1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,270
Don Giovanni, episode one: the man in the cloak.

2
00:00:04,190 --> 00:00:18,230
Night in Seville. In the courtyard of the Commendatore's palace, a servant paces with a lantern. Leporello. He grumbles Notte e giorno faticar: toiling night and day for a master who never thanks him. I want to be the gentleman, he says, not the servant. Then he hears footsteps and hides.

3
00:00:19,550 --> 00:00:31,240
Out of the house runs a man wrapped in a long cloak, hiding his face. Clinging to him is Donna Anna, the Commendatore's daughter. Don't hope to escape, she cries, unless you kill me. Help! Who is this man? He will not say. She will not let go.

4
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:47,730
Then her father comes, an old man with a sword and a light. Fight me, he says. The stranger refuses: he will not fight an old man. The Commendatore insists. Two blades in the dark, a few strokes, and the old man falls. Before he dies, the stranger watches him, almost curious. Then he and Leporello slip away into the night.

5
00:00:49,250 --> 00:00:58,380
Donna Anna comes back with her betrothed, Don Ottavio, and finds her father in his blood. She faints. When she wakes, she pushes Ottavio away: Fuggi, crudele, fuggi, go, cruel man.

6
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:07,350
He is the only one left to her, he answers, a husband and a father. Then swear, she says. Over the body they swear revenge on a man whose face nobody saw.
